TITLE='Authentic title "You\'ll Stop Working BEFORE 50 Once You Understand This" is a curiosity-gap promise with an age anchor. The script delivers the anchor (one number: savings rate) within the first minute and the title promise is honoured, with an explicit late caveat that a 50% savings rate is far easier at high incomes. The "before 50" framing rests on the savings-rate table, which assumes a 5% real return and the 4% rule the video later says is too generous.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White field. Left: the recurring cartoon man smiling, hands on hips, surrounded by falling dollar bills. Centre: an office desk with computer and paper stacks crossed out by a red X. Right: a large black headline "RETIRE BEFORE 50" with a black arrow pointing at the desk. At 320x180 the headline stays legible, "50" dominates; the red X stays visible; the bills become small green marks. The thumbnail text is a paraphrase of the title, not an extra claim; it shows outcome, not mechanism.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator early-retirement explainer built around two composite coworkers (Robert, who saved ~half his pay, and Zoe, who out-earned him and spent it): hook, savings-rate table, double effect of spending less, 4% rule and a 2026 valuation caveat moving it to ~3.5%, three levers and lifestyle creep, account order, Munger compounding quote, early-access paths (Roth ladder, 72(t), Roth contributions), ACA subsidy strategy with a 2026 caveat, Robert\'s compounding inflection, a school-community promotion, and an honest income caveat. Arithmetic is internally consistent; main errors are the incomplete 72(t) rule and the loose 3.5%/30x pairing.'
BEATS=['Hook: highest earner never retires, Robert vs Zoe.','Disclaimer and roadmap.','Savings rate as the one number; 10% to 75% table.','Double lever of spending less; $60,000 example; $500,000 earner at zero.','4% rule, Bengen 1994, 25x.','Longer retirement and valuations: 3.5% and 30x.','Three levers; lifestyle creep and hedonic adaptation.','Account order: 401(k) match, HSA, IRA, brokerage.','Munger: first $100,000.','Early access: Roth ladder, 72(t), Roth contributions.','Health insurance before 65; income-based subsidies; 2026 caveat.','Robert\'s inflection around year 12.','School-community promotion.','Honest catch: income matters; 10% to 20% saves ~14 years; close.']
